      "actionId": null,
      "candidateId": "v002",
      "details": {
        "outcome": "passed",
        "review": "The five flags locate the input mesh, the B/H key, the frame lock on S, and both moving-axis meshes. The gear ratios, front views, input, outputs and four choices are legible. Independent reading: The fixed-center external 20T/30T mesh reverses A. B and its keyed carrier H turn CCW. The frame holds S. Relative to H, S turns CW. Two external meshes through I give P the same relative direction at 24/36 of the carrier speed. Restoring the carrier motion leaves P spinning CCW at one third of the carrier speed while H orbits CCW."
      },
      "evidenceRefs": []
    },
